  <div class="philosophy-heading"><span class="section-kicker">Philosophy & interests</span><h2 class="section-title" id="philosophy-title">What matters to me.</h2></div>
  <div class="principles">
    <div><span>01</span><div><h3>Open work</h3><p>Research should leave something other people can run, inspect, and build on. I publish tools and experiments with that in mind.</p></div></div>
    <div><span>02</span><div><h3>Ideas across fields</h3><p>I like working with people who see the same problem from software engineering, formal methods, or security. Those conversations change the tools I build.</p></div></div>
    <div><span>03</span><div><h3>Hard systems</h3><p>I’m interested in testing systems where simple input generators fall short: structured formats, stateful protocols, and AI systems that need to behave reliably in practice.</p></div></div>
  </div>
